Fundamentals
- Domain name  : human-readable label (variable example: google.com)
- IP address   : numeric locator computers use (IPv4: 32-bit, IPv6: 128-bit)
- DNS role     : resolves name → address so the browser can open a TCP/IP connection
- Flow         : User types name → Browser queries DNS → DNS returns IP → Browser connects to that IP
